  "description": {
    "short": "Drag faceted gem pieces onto an 8x8 lattice, clear rows and columns, chain combos and keep your daily streak alive.",
    "long": "Gem Lattice is a calm, crunchy block puzzle. Three gem pieces wait in the tray; drag one onto the 8x8 lattice and it snaps into place with a ghost preview, lifted above your finger on touch screens so you can always see where it lands. Fill a whole row or column and the gems shatter in a burst of light. Clearing several lines at once multiplies your score, and consecutive clearing moves build a streak that multiplies it further, so planning two or three placements ahead pays off. Wipe the entire board for a big bonus. The run ends only when none of the remaining pieces fit anywhere.\n\nPlay Classic for an endless run against your saved best, or take on the Daily Board: a seeded starting layout and piece sequence that is the same for every player on the same day, with a streak counter for coming back. Adventure mode has 30 hand-tuned levels with clear goals such as score targets, line counts, gold gems and multi-line combos. Every level awards up to three stars with the same simple rules, a level-start card explains the goal in plain words, and the results screen shows exactly which stars you earned or missed so you can retry for a perfect run. Progress, stars and settings are saved on your device, the game never advances on its own, and the sound toggle is always one tap away.",
    "controls": "Drag a piece from the tray onto the board with mouse or touch. Full rows and columns clear. Esc or P pauses, M mutes, Enter or R tries again.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Is there a daily puzzle?",
        "a": "Yes. A new seeded Daily Board every day, the same for every player, with a streak counter."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I earn three stars?",
        "a": "Complete the level goal, finish within the move limit, and reach the score or tighter move target shown on the level-start card."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it save my progress?",
        "a": "Yes. Best scores, stars, unlocked levels and settings are saved on your device."
      }
    ]
  },
